      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Kod'Taz, Broken Trial Grounds [zone=249]\n**Who:**\n- Tublik Narwethar [npc=15988]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 65\n**Maximum Level:** | 130\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n**Quest Items:**\n- Fragment of the High Temple [item=28316]\n- Icon of the Altar [item=30451]\n- Sliver of the High Temple [Unfinished]\n- Sliver of the High Temple [Finished]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Ikkinz, Chambers of Destruction [zone=248]\n- Qvic, Prayer Grounds of Calling [zone=254]\n- Uqua, the Ocean God Chantry [zone=252]\n- Yxtta, Pulpit of Exiles [zone=250]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Jerimo Jiao [npc=15178]\n- Keeper of the Altar [npc=14749]\n- Sentinel of the Altar [npc=17463]\n- a pile of bones - Destruction [npc=21432]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Gates of Discord Progression #5: Crafting an Icon of the Altar [quest=7597]\n- Gates of Discord Progression #7: Access to Txevu [quest=2917]\n- Ikkinz Raid #4: Chambers of Destruction [quest=3464]\n**Era:** | !Gates of Discord\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Jul 3 19:11:27 2014\nModified: Mon Jul 13 23:06:23 2026 | | **_Note: If you're Level 62+, you have access to Qvic by default. To gain official access (or enter it under level), all you need is a \"Sliver of the High Temple\" from the fourth Ikkinz raid (and a turn-in) and a \"Fragment of the High Temple\" from the Uqua raid. You don't need any of the progression leading up to requesting those raids; you only need those two specific items._**\n_This part of Gates of Discord progression follows your **construction of an Icon of the Altar** [quest=7597] (note that some elements of progression can be completed outside of the order outlined here, which is but one path you can take)._\n\n---\n\n!!\n\n---\n\n**Sliver of the High Temple**\nYou say, 'Hail, Tublik Narwethar'\nTublik Narwethar says 'There you are! I've been waiting for you. I've examined the final glyph on the Icon of the Altar and it seems to suggest that there must have been a final battle between the trusik priests and a keeper of some sort. I can't quite determine what the keeper is, but I imagine it won't be friendly. Before you enter the keeper's inner chambers, you'll need to present your Icon of the Altar to a stone [sentinel] standing guard outside. By all accounts, this seems to be the same path that the priests had to take as well.'\nYou say, 'What about this sentinel?'\nTublik Narwethar says 'Like the keeper, I don't know what you should expect with the sentinel, so be prepared for anything. I must send you on your way now and wish you whatever luck a poor dwarf can muster. Fortune has treated you well so far... let's hope it continues.'\n_Head to the top of the giant temple in the zone's northwest and see the \"Sentinel of the Altar\" (/loc 620, 1600, -330). Hand it the Icon of the Altar to initiate the final Ikkinz raid expedition._\n_Complete the raid expedition **Ikkinz, Antechamber of Destruction** [quest=3464] and loot the \"Sliver of the High Temple\" from the pile of bones that spawns after the Keeper of the Altar's death._\n_Hand in the \"Sliver of the High Temple\" to Tublik Narwethar:_\nTublik Narwethar says 'You've exceed all my expectations. This key is only the first of what looks to be three needed... needed for what I wonder? I imagine you'll find out more as you continue your adventures. Seek out Brevik in the Abysmal Sea should you discover anything else. He is one of the Wayfarers Brotherhood's resident geomancer adepts. He's not yet fully skilled, but he has much in the way of knowledge of the craft already and learning more each day. He will no doubt have more information for you. For now, I bid you good luck and farewell, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_!'\n_You receive back a different version of the \"Sliver of the High Temple\"._\n\n---\n\n**Fragment of the High Temple**\n_To obtain a \"Fragment of the High Temple\", all you need to do is complete the raid expedition \" **Uqua, the Ocean God Chantry** [quest=4479]\" (see link for details), and hail the \"Specter of Barxt\" that spawns at the end._\n_The Uqua raid is given out by Jerimo Jiao in the southwestern part of Yxtta, the Pulpit of Exiles._\n\n---\n\n**Entering Qvic, Prayer Grounds of Calling**\n_Once you've obtained **both** a \" **Sliver of the High Temple** [item=30339]\" and a **Fragment of the High Temple** [item=28316], have these items in your inventory while you zone into Qvic via Kod'Taz or Yxtta. Upon zoning in, you will be /keyed for the zone._\n_From here, you can speak with Madronoa (far northwestern corner of Natimbi) to zone into Qvic:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Madronoa'\nMadronoa says 'Hello \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, how are you today? My name is Madronoa and I have recently returned from the Prayer Grounds of Calling. A group of young adventurers such as yourself led me there some time ago. While there I learned of the geomantic barrier that prevents others from entering and I've learned how to channel the energy of that barrier to teleport those such as yourself there. However, you must have acquired the Fragment and Sliver of the High Temple to be able to get past the unseen force preventing adventurers from entering. If you have both of these pieces and to travel to Qvic, I shall create a portal for you.'\nYou say, 'I wish to travel to Qvic.'\nMadronoa says 'Very well, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Safe travels to you.'\nA flash of light occurs as you are teleported away from this place.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered Qvic, Prayer Grounds of Calling.\nThe magical barrier protecting Qvic softens as you pass through it.\n\n---\n\n**Moving On**\n_You can now move onto the next part of Gates of Discord progression: **Access to Txevu** [quest=2917]._",
